@* The shared "Psalm numbering" guide section. Each guide supplies its own opening paragraph (which scheme it uses);
   the explanation of how the Hebrew and Vulgate schemes differ is common to all. *@
<GuideSection Title="Psalm numbering">
    @ChildContent
    <p>
        The two schemes differ because the Vulgate joins Psalms 9 and 10, and Psalms 114 and 115, into single psalms,
        while it splits Psalms 116 and 147 into two each. As a result, most psalms from 10 through 147 are one number lower in the Vulgate.
        Psalms 1 through 8 and 148 through 150 are numbered the same in both.
    </p>
</GuideSection>

